        description:
          "How to get beyond the hype and start extracting breakthrough value from AI Every company is talking about AI, but they’re not all getting value from AI. Having built and sold an AI-enabled tech company, I know first hand the ones that are view AI as a people challenge first, and a technology challenge second. That’s because with technology like AI, companies don’t change, people do. For example, according to recent research from 2024, the companies getting the most value from AI are spending twice as much on people as they are on algos and tech. Gen AI “high performers’ do a much better job of helping everyone understand value and risks of AI in their daily job (52%) compared to those not getting value (only 21%)… this is what I mean by people first, tech second. In this dynamic, provocative and practically useful session we will: Unpack the ‘why’, the ‘what’ and the ‘how’ of leading edge Gen AI technologies and share compelling, industry- and role-relevant case studies of how companies are getting value. Look at the human element of AI integration, and how ensure that our teams are set up and structured to adopt and get value from these new tools. Unpack the practical risk management and governance mindsets and frameworks required to avoid pitfalls and perils while still making progress. Draw on Dom’s first-hand experiences building and selling an AI-enabled technology company to bring a real on-the-ground perspective the conversation.",
